{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>For the midwives.</b> Rav and Shmuel — one says: a woman and her daughter, Yocheved and Miriam; and one says: a daughter-in-law and her mother-in-law, Yocheved and Elisheva. Another interpretation: למילדת is written defectively, without vav — this teaches that there was only one midwife, and that is Yocheved. But Miriam was a young girl and was not a midwife, rather she would פועה ['call out / puff'] to the infant, and therefore the Sages said: 'Puah — this is Miriam.' From the Maharam Moshe Cohen. Another interpretation: she would פועה to the infant in the womb and call to it, 'Come out,' and it would come out."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The word למילדות ('for the midwives') is the lemma; the comment notes that למילדת ('for the midwife') appears in the verse without the vav of the plural form. The verb פועה is left untranslated as it functions as a name-wordplay; it may mean calling out, puffing, or coaxing."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:26.947220745Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}